set.body:
Goal: introduce the universal mathematical program before migrating named methods.

Deliverables:
- typed parameter blocks whose variables are directed maps, not anonymous matrices;
- a closed BaseObjective ADT covering generalized Rayleigh-Ritz, cross-SVD/bilinear association, trace ratio, ratio trace, and sequential cross-regression;
- typed compression expressions, normalization constraints, exact parameterizations, penalties, hard constraints, and a result-semantics contract;
- result equivalence, representative-selection rule, numerical identifiability evidence, solver guarantee, provenance, and fitted transformations;
- lightweight named builders compile to OperatorProgram; no method-specific numerical universe;
- a minimal serialization seam used by multivar-ir.

Boundary: this issue defines the skeleton and smooth spectral cases. General target/functionals/sets, operator policies, nonsmooth lowering, and ModelSpec expansion belong to the separate variational epic.

Acceptance:
- GPCA, LDA, CCA/PLS, and multiset programs can be represented without model-specific escape callbacks;
- exhaustive tests cover every BaseObjective constructor and result-contract variant;
- invalid space/orientation/normalization combinations fail at construction;
- shared JVM and JS suites pass with direct dense reference checks.
